*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   SCREEN VIEWPORT f, id {AT x,y} {SIZE w,h} {CONTENT cw,ch} {TITLE t} {NOBORDER}
*
*   is compiled into
*
*   call !screen_viewport(f, id, x, y, w, h, cw, ch, title, noborder, ret, status)
*
*     f id      the form and the widget's name in it (as SCREEN LABEL)
*     x y       the top left corner, as SCREEN CONTAINER, default 1,1
*     w h       its size, border included, default 30 by 10
*     cw ch     the size of the sheet the widgets are placed on, default what shows (nothing to scroll)
*     title     shown in its top border
*     noborder  no border is drawn and the whole rectangle is the inside
*     status    0 added; 1 not (ELSE)
*
*   A container (SCREEN CONTAINER) whose inside is a window on a sheet cw by ch.  The widgets added after SCREEN IN f, id are
*   placed on the sheet (0,0 is its top left cell) and only the part in the window is drawn and takes the mouse.  A bar
*   appears in the right column when the sheet is higher than the window, and in the bottom row when it is wider.  Scroll it
*   with the arrow keys, Page Up and Down, Home and End while the viewport has the focus (it is in the Tab ring), the wheel
*   anywhere over it (Shift-wheel for columns), a click on a bar, a drag of its thumb, or SCREEN SCROLL.  A widget that takes
*   the focus is scrolled into view.  SCREEN GET answers the first column and row shown, from 0, with a value mark between;
*   a WAIT gives a scroll as the change event of the viewport's id with that as its data.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine screen_viewport(f, id, ax, ay, sw, sh, cw, ch, title, noborder, ret, status)
$catalog !screen_viewport

   ret = ''
   status = 1
   w = collection()
   w{'id'} = id
   w{'type'} = 'viewport'
   w{'title'} = title
   x = 1
   y = 1
   vw = 30
   vh = 10
   if ax # '' then x = ax + 0
   if ay # '' then y = ay + 0
   if sw # '' then vw = sw + 0
   if sh # '' then vh = sh + 0
   w{'x'} = x
   w{'y'} = y
   w{'w'} = vw
   w{'h'} = vh
   if cw # '' then w{'cw'} = cw + 0
   if ch # '' then w{'ch'} = ch + 0
   w{'border'} = if noborder # '' then 0 else 1
   call $sl_viewport('init', w, '', '', r)
   call $sl_wadd(f, w, ok)
   if ok then status = 0

   return
end

* END-CODE
